<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Server debug tools for viewing runtime information about the BEAM VM. Requires server administrator role. Read-only, no side effects."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_question}>{dgettext("help_commands", "When to Use It")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Use it to check a running server: how many channels are live right now, which ones they are, and how the server uses memory. Nothing is changed, so it is safe to run at any time."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_code}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Syntax")}</.help_h4>
<pre>/admin debug connections
/admin debug processes
/admin debug memory</pre>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tag}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Subcommands")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>connections</code> {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "— Show the number of running channel processes"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>processes</code> {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "— List running channel processes by name, with their process ids"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>memory</code>
    {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "— Show BEAM VM memory usage breakdown (total, processes, atoms, binary, ETS)"
    )}
  </li>
</ul>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_commands", "How It Works")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Each reply appears as system lines in the window you are viewing."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  <code>connections</code> {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "reports how many channel processes are running. It does not count client connections."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "The %{sub} subcommand lists each running channel by name, with its process id. An unregistered channel stops its process when its last member leaves, so it drops off this list.",
    sub: "processes"
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "The %{sub} subcommand shows sizes in megabytes for total memory, processes, ETS, atoms, binaries and loaded code.",
    sub: "memory"
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Rules & Limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_commands", "You must be a server administrator and identified with NickServ")}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Other users get an error and nothing is shown")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Without a subcommand, you see the usage line")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_commands", "An unknown subcommand gets an error that lists the valid ones")}
  </li>
</ul>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Examples")}</.help_h4>
<pre>/admin debug connections
/admin debug memory
/admin debug processes</pre>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_commands", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-admin">{dgettext("help_commands", "/admin")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-admin-server">{dgettext("help_commands", "/admin server")}</.help_link>
</p>
